      "level": 1,
      "content": "Copy a file to another file"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Copying a file might sound like a difficult program. But it is simpler than you think."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "To copy the contents of one file to another,"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "we will read the contents of a file you want to copy",
        "then write the contents of the file to another file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We will copy the contents of message.txt to output.txt."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "message.txt",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We will follow the following steps:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. import java.io.FileReader and java.io.FileWriter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As we want to read and write files, we must import both java.io.FileReader and java.io.FileWriter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. read the file contents"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We must read the contents of the file we want to copy."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "content": "FileReader copy = new FileReader(\"message.txt\");\ncopy.read(contents);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. write the contents to file"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "content": "FileWriter paste = new FileWriter(\"output.txt\");\npaste.write(contents);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "4. Close the file"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Once we perform file operations, it's a good practice to close the file."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
